[node name="Founder" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("1")

; Layout is the authority for position (D-77). Every child is a slot the screen draws:
; its name is what the code asks for, its position is where that lands, and its size is
; what it occupies. Names carry no dots -- Godot forbids them in node names, so they are
; short names rather than manifest ids. Drag these in the 2D editor and the game follows;
; nothing converts them back. The manifest still owns sizes, anchors and draw order, so
; a ColorRect's size here is a visual aid, not the truth — resize the manifest entry.
; Slots with art are Sprite2D showing the real texture; the rest are ColorRect boxes
; standing in for text. A Sprite2D of chrome is scaled 0.5 because chrome ships at 2x (D-76).
; The portrait, badge and roster show one example -- content picks the real one at runtime.
